#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fold

#% text
# `fold(f, x, xs)` gives `f(...f(f(x, xs[1]), xs[2])..., xs[n])`: the elements of `xs` combined from the left, starting from `x`.

#% text
# `fold(f, xs)` starts from the first element of `xs`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `f` takes two arguments: the value so far and the next element.

#% item
# `fold(f, x, [])` is `x`; `fold(f, [])` is a failure, since there is no first element.

#% item
# `fold_list` gives every intermediate value, not only the last.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fold(f, x, [a, b, c])
#% output
#= f(f(f(x, a), b), c)

#% cell
fold((s, k) => s + k, 0, range(10))
#% output
#= 55

#% cell
fold((a, b) => a*b, [1, 2, 3, 4, 5])
#% output
#= 120

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Any kind of value can be carried along, here a list:

#% cell
fold((acc, k) => append(acc, k^2), [], [1, 2, 3])
#% output
#= [1, 4, 9]

#% text
# An empty list gives the start value:

#% cell
fold(f, x, [])
#% output
#= x

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A polynomial evaluated by Horner's scheme from its coefficients, highest first:

#% cell
fold((acc, c) => acc*x + c, 0, [2, -3, 0, 5])
#% output
#= 5 + (-3 + 2*x)*x^2

#% cell
fold((acc, c) => acc*2 + c, 0, [2, -3, 0, 5])
#% output
#= 9

#% text
# The greatest common divisor of many numbers, two at a time:

#% cell
fold(gcd, [84, 126, 210])
#% output
#= 42

#% text
# A number from its digits:

#% cell
fold((acc, d) => 10*acc + d, 0, [3, 1, 4, 1, 5])
#% output
#= 31415

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The last value of `fold_list` is the value of `fold`:

#% cell
last(fold_list((a, b) => a + b, 0, [4, 5, 6])) == fold((a, b) => a + b, 0, [4, 5, 6])
#% output
#= true

#% text
# For a sum, `total` does the same directly:

#% cell
total(range(10))
#% output
#= 55

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Without a start value, an empty list has nothing to start from:

#% cell
fold((a, b) => a + b, [])
#% output
#! failure(index, 1, 0)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fold_list`, `nest`, `accumulate`, `total`, `map`
